    "message": "KS-723: declare GET /api/anchors/tx/{txHash} in the published OpenAPI contract\n\nRefs KS-723\n\nGET /api/anchors/tx/:txHash has been routed since services/anchoring/src/index.ts:1089\nand answers { success: true, data: <one anchor> }, but the published OpenAPI document\ndid not declare it. An undeclared operation is invisible offline: the contract suites\nhave nothing to generate against it and a change to its response shape breaks no test.\nIt is now registered on the shared registry anchoring.openapi.ts populates on import,\nso npm run generate-openapi emits it. No route and no handler is changed.\n\nNARROWING, not closing: KS-723 covers the remaining ~157 routed-but-undocumented /api\noperations and this declares ONE. Stuart named two /api/anchors reads on the ticket on\n2026-09-29; the sibling GET /api/anchors/{id} (index.ts:827) is deliberately left out,\nbecause declaring it on this registry would make the gateway answer 405 to two LIVE\nPOST routes sharing the prefix. It is not rejected. KS-723 stays OPEN for it.\n\nRed-first, by assertion: with the test section applied and the product hunk absent the\ncell file is rc 1, 3 failed / 2 passed of 5 EXECUTED - TX1, TX2, TX3 red on real\nAssertionErrors, the file's own two controls green. Five executed, so an assertion red\nand not a load failure. With the product hunk: rc 0, 5 passed of 5.\n\nanchoring unit suite 27 files / 357 tests to 28 / 362, delta exactly +1 file / +5\ntests, 0 NEW reds. One failure at BOTH ends: threadTokenMint.test.ts, the pre-existing\n@lucid-evolution red recorded at BACKLOG.md:182 on develop. Not introduced here.\n\nThe spec was REGENERATED, never pasted: generate-openapi rc 0, 310 paths,\ndocs/openapi/secuura-api.yaml 1,351,218 to 1,354,452 bytes by wc -c, /api/anchors/tx/\n0 to 1 occurrence. check:openapi rc 0; drift control, a one-byte YAML edit, gives rc 1\nCHECK FAIL and was restored cmp-identical. The generator's own \"1349709 bytes\" is a\nCHARACTER count (2,375 non-ASCII characters); the figures above are wc -c.\n\ntsc rc 0, and the claim is narrower than that reads. Its control FIRES on the product\nfile: a planted TS2322 in anchoring.openapi.ts gives rc 2, restored byte-identical.\nBut services/anchoring/tsconfig.json excludes src/__tests__, so the new test file is\nNOT in the program (0 under --listFilesOnly) and the same plant inside it still gives\nrc 0. The new test file is TYPE-UNCHECKED: NOT RUN, not covered. tsconfig not widened.\n\nBoth platform-k documents carry a new block in this commit: flow 16. between 14. and\n18. (numbered h2s ascending, 17 h2 total), cheat sheet a new LAST section after\nKS 1005, per the ruling. No stated timing row is amended and no tier budget moves:\n0 stated timings cover an anchoring unit suite at the base (must-hit controls auth\n89/81 and anchoring 18/19, so the zeroes are measurements).\n\nThe held carve declares @@ -406,7 +406,44 @@ and git apply refuses it rc 128 corrupt\npatch at line 57. Counting the hunk body, 51 lines, gives old 7 (matching the shipped\n-406,7) and new 50; the shipped 44 is short by 6. A header-fixed copy differing in\nexactly that one line was applied and the held artefact re-hashed unchanged.\n\nNOT COVERED: no live sweep (skill 5f), so KS-723 does not move to Done on this change\naccount and stays open for the second endpoint. That the gateway serves the newly\ndeclared operation, and that the runtime response really matches the declared\nenvelope, are both UNMEASURED: the cells read the generated document, not a live\nresponse. The four platform suites (Schemathesis, Akto, Playwright, k6) were NOT run.",
